msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:55
msgid "How do I buy a Mattermost Cloud subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:57
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud subscriptions are offered as an annual subscription. "
"Contact a `Mattermost Expert <https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_ to"
" buy a new subscription, or to renew, change, or cancel your existing "
"subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:59
msgid ""
"If you’re currently using a Mattermost Cloud trial, contact a `Mattermost"
" Expert <https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_ to upgrade to "
"Mattermost Enterprise. Your plan immediately changes to your upgraded "
"plan. You will be invoiced as specified in your sales agreement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:62
msgid "What is the minimum number of users I can purchase on a subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:64
msgid ""
"The minimum purchase for a Mattermost license subscription is 100 users, "
"with no set maximum. You can buy as many user seats as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:67
msgid "Is Mattermost Cloud subject to taxes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:69
msgid ""
"Yes. Mattermost reserves the right to assess applicable taxes as required"
" by local law. Depending on location, you may be charged transaction "
"taxes when purchasing our product. `Prices "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`_ on our website are exclusive of sales"
" tax or VAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:72
msgid "Where does instance and data reside?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:74
msgid ""
"Dedicated instance and data, including logs and backups, resides in the "
"**AWS us-east-1 region**, located in Virginia, United States."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:76
msgid ""
"For data residency options outside of the US, contact a `Mattermost "
"Expert <https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_, or work with a "
"`Mattermost partner <https://mattermost.com/partners/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:79
msgid "When will more region support be available?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:81
msgid ""
":doc:`Mattermost Cloud Dedicated </product-overview/cloud-dedicated>` "
"will support data residency based on feedback from our customers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:83
msgid ""
"If you require your data to reside in an area outside of the United "
"States, please contact a `Mattermost Expert <https://mattermost.com"
"/contact-sales/>`_ or consider deploying one of our `self-hosted options "
"<https://mattermost.com/download/>`_ that provides you with full control "
"of your data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:86
msgid ""
"Do you provide cross-region failover in the event of an outage in AWS us-"
"east-1 region?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:88
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud is hosted in AWS us-east-1 region. Cross-region failover"
" is planned, but not yet in the roadmap. If you have feedback or require "
"cross-region failover, please reach out to a `Mattermost Expert "
"<https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:91
msgid "Is Mattermost Cloud a dedicated instance running on AWS systems?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:93
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud Dedicated can be deployed as a dedicated Mattermost "
"environment running with separate infrastructure for your requirements "
"(e.g., separate database, separate VMs, separate Kubernetes cluster)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:96
msgid "How is customer data in Mattermost Cloud Dedicated encrypted?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:98
msgid ""
"Mattermost uses AWS-provided functionality to enable encryption-at-rest "
"for both databases and file stores. See `Encrypting Amazon RDS resources "
"- Amazon Relational Database Service "
"<https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Overview.Encryption.html>`_"
" and `Protecting data using server-side encryption - Amazon Simple "
"Storage Service <https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide"
"/serv-side-encryption.html>`_ for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:100
msgid ""
"Whether customer data should be stored in Mattermost Cloud depends "
"heavily on the nature of the data and compliance requirements. We "
"recommend that customers set up their own internal policies or controls "
"around what can and cannot be put into Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:103
msgid "Are S3-managed keys used for server-side encryption?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:105
msgid ""
"Yes, with Mattermost Cloud Dedicated. You can also bring your own keys "
"for database and Amazon S3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:108
msgid "Are you SOC2 Type 2 certified?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:110
msgid "Yes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:113
msgid "Who is responsible for server maintenance and upgrades?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:115
msgid ""
"For Mattermost Cloud deployments, Mattermost is responsible for regular "
"security patches, software updates/releases, performance tuning, and "
"ensuring uptime commitments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:117
msgid ""
"Mattermost performs monthly upgrades to your instance with the latest "
"patch release during your preferred maintenance window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:119
msgid ""
"Mattermost may conduct unscheduled maintenance to address high-severity "
"issues affecting the security, availability, or reliability of your "
"instance. Maintenance windows are announced in advance on "
"https://status.mattermost.com/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:121
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud uses a Cloud-First Release Strategy with Ring-Based "
"staged releases aligned to Mattermost licenses with a 24 hour soak time "
"for :doc:`Mattermost Cloud Dedicated </product-overview/cloud-dedicated>`"
" and for Enterprise customers using :doc:`Mattermost Cloud Shared "
"</product-overview/cloud-shared>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:124
msgid "Can I use a custom URL at my organization's domain?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:126
msgid ""
"No. Custom URLs are not currently supported for Mattermost Cloud "
"deployments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-subscriptions.rst:128
msgid ""
"`Book a live demo <https://mattermost.com/request-demo/>`_  or `talk to a"
" Mattermost expert <https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_ to explore "
"tailored solutions for your organization's secure collaboration needs. Or"
" try Mattermost yourself with a `1-hour preview <https://mattermost.com"
"/sign-up/>`_ for instant access to a live sandbox environment."
msgstr ""

